From b56b37e87ffaf6d70dd9fe589ec959e4a9dfddc0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yuichi Kusakabe <yuichi_kusakabe@jp.honda>
Date: Wed, 08 Jul 2026 00:00:00 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] xrun: compile without CONFIG_SDHC (DomD owns the SD)


With the SoC SDHCI passed through to DomD (DomD-as-toolstack), the Zephyr Dom0
disables CONFIG_SDHC and CONFIG_SDHC_BUFFER_ALIGNMENT no longer exists.
Provide a safe fallback so the xrun storage path keeps compiling; it is unused
at runtime in this topology.

Assisted-by: Claude Code:claude-opus-4-8
Signed-off-by: Yuichi Kusakabe <yuichi_kusakabe@jp.honda>
Upstream-Status: Pending [xen-troops/zephyr-xrun]
---
diff --git a/src/storage.c b/src/storage.c
index 4452fd7..8ee601d 100644
--- a/src/storage.c
+++ b/src/storage.c
@@ -11,6 +11,13 @@
 
 #include <storage.h>
 
+/* SDHC is disabled (the SD is passed through to DomD),
+ * so CONFIG_SDHC_BUFFER_ALIGNMENT does not exist; keep compiling with a safe
+ * default (the storage path is unused at runtime in this topology). */
+#ifndef CONFIG_SDHC_BUFFER_ALIGNMENT
+#define CONFIG_SDHC_BUFFER_ALIGNMENT 4
+#endif
+
 LOG_MODULE_REGISTER(storage);
 
 #if CONFIG_XRUN_STORAGE_DMA_DEBOUNCE > 0
